{"parentUuid":"6d56721f-c474-4eea-8d92-727364e2b30f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JqEC2XWYB6WCEyNpmGP5VL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QH27gL6CDy7nLSy54qbWH9","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"or-tools\" 9.15 breaking changes callback API SAT solver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":370,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2514,"cache_read_input_tokens":23872,"output_tokens":758,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2514},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":370,"output_tokens":758,"cache_read_input_tokens":23872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2514,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot1TqAvhgPWzc8wd39u","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d46d285-fe71-41ca-b6c0-6348870f07ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:27.600Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c3bf4306-4ea1-46f7-934e-8bfea68d1f51","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNvgZmESs1MpKiCnsv4JwG","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools v9.13 Release Notes\n\nBased on the GitHub release page, here are the key changes for v9.13:\n\n## Platform Changes\n- \"Drop Python 3.8 support\"\n- \".Net 6.0 support\" was discontinued in favor of .Net 8.0\n- Fedora 42 support added\n- Java 8 may be dropped in favor of Java 11\n\n## Dependency Updates\n**C++:** abseil-cpp 20250512.0, Protobuf v31.0, HiGHS v1.10.0, SCIP v922\n\n**Python:** typing-extensions dependencies added\n\n## CP-SAT Improvements\nThe release notes highlight several solver enhancements:\n- \"Improvements to the no_overlap_2d constraint (presolve, propagation, and cuts)\"\n- Feasibility jump and violation local search were optimized\n- Precedences with bounds detection for use in presolve, propagation, and cuts\n- \"Deep improvements to routing cuts. Detect transition between nodes. Detect capacity constraints\"\n- Scheduling cuts improvements\n- Better clause sharing in shared_tree and portfolio search\n- sat_runner now parses .pb and .wbo files\n- \"Python: better support for float coefficient and bounds\"\n- General bug fixes and performance improvements\n\n## Known Issues\nTwo issues are documented: libscip linkage errors on Mac and ComputeMinSumOfWeightedEndMins errors."}]},"uuid":"04628766-60a2-4728-afba-0e04955aeb73","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:27.858Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3bf4306-4ea1-46f7-934e-8bfea68d1f51","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d46d285-fe71-41ca-b6c0-6348870f07ec","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QH27gL6CDy7nLSy54qbWH9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" 9.15 breaking changes callback API SAT solver\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/solver.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/solver.md\"},{\"title\":\"Expose linear solver callback to .Net · Issue #2603 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2603\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Lanzamientos · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://translate.google.com/translate?u=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fgoogle%2For-tools%2Freleases&hl=es&sl=en&tl=es&client=srp\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/ufunc/api/solvers/ortools.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools version 9.15 and breaking changes related to the callback API for the SAT solver:\n\n## Key Breaking Change in v9.15\n\nThere is a breaking argument change in CpSolver.Solve() callback (issue #4988). This is a significant API change that users upgrading to version 9.15 need to be aware of.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe CP-SAT solver has received significant improvements, including API changes, performance enhancements, and expanded functionality for constraints and linear expressions in recent releases.\n\nCP-SAT callbacks in Python, Java, .NET can slow down search performance a lot as it is possible that search will continue until the time limit is crossed even as the problems has been closed before.\n\nFor more detailed information about the specific callback API changes, you may want to check the official GitHub release notes or changelog for OR-Tools v9.15, as the search results reference issue #4988 which would contain the implementation details of the breaking change.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2347b3d3-5b3c-4d2f-994f-28fb1cbc0813","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:33.188Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1d46d285-fe71-41ca-b6c0-6348870f07ec","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"364a45d0-b720-432f-b6aa-9348218dd33d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Agyu3CAVJYdoVBkPRdbAVq","type":"tool_result","content":"# OR-Tools v9.12 Release Notes Summary\n\nBased on the GitHub release page, here are the key highlights:\n\n## Platform Changes\n- \"This will be the last release to support Python3.8\" and Java 1.8\n- Added Python 3.13 support\n- Introduced muslinux wheel packages\n- Windows libraries now distributed as DLLs\n\n## Dependency Updates\nThe release upgraded multiple libraries including Protobuf 29.3, HiGHS 1.9.0, and SCIP v920. Dependencies are now \"seperated shared libraries\" rather than bundled together.\n\n## Breaking Changes\nThe old graph classes (`EbertGraph`, `StarGraph`, `ForwardEbertGraph`, `ForwardStarGraph`) were removed in favor of `ReverseArcListGraph<>` and `ListGraph<>`.\n\n## CP-SAT Enhancements\nNotable improvements include:\n- Enhanced no_overlap_2d layer with better propagation and cuts\n- Rewrote hint transformation during presolve to preserve feasible hints\n- Optimized Python expression handling\n- Improved shared tree workers with job affinity\n- Added scheduling sample code\n\n## Additional Features\n- Linear Solver gained `WriteModelToMpsFile` method across Java, Python, and .NET\n- Math Opt now supports Xpress\n- Model Builder added HiGHS support\n\n## Known Issues\nThree documented issues affect macOS Intel wheels, MathOpt tests, and graph shortest path tests."}]},"uuid":"e783a796-97ba-4d3d-a9da-c222ed68de2b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:36.175Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"364a45d0-b720-432f-b6aa-9348218dd33d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6d56721f-c474-4eea-8d92-727364e2b30f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8fGniwaeUVKRBhH5UUj6Z","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recent Parameter Additions and Changes in SatParameters\n\nBased on the provided proto file, here are notable recent additions and experimental parameters:\n\n## no_overlap_2d Constraints\n- **use_try_edge_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d** (bool, default=false, tag 299): \"Try edge reasoning\" heuristic\n- **use_linear3_for_no_overlap_2d_precedences** (bool, default=true, tag 323): Leverages linear constraints for precedence detection\n- **maximum_regions_to_split_in_disconnected_no_overlap_2d** (int32, default=0, tag 315): Bin packing expansion for disconnected regions\n\n## Cumulative & Scheduling\n- **use_conservative_scale_overload_checker** (bool, default=false, tag 286): Energy-based heuristic using super-additive functions\n- **use_dynamic_precedence_in_cumulative** (bool, default=false, tag 268): \"Experimental\" branching on interval precedences\n\n## Shared Tree Search (Experimental Portfolio)\n- **shared_tree_num_workers** (int32, default=-1, tag 235): Distributed tree exploration\n- **shared_tree_balance_tolerance** (int32, default=1, tag 305): Depth tolerance for balanced splitting\n- **shared_tree_split_min_dtime** (double, default=0.1, tag 328): Contention limiting between split proposals\n\n## LP & Cuts\n- **add_rlt_cuts** (bool, default=true, tag 279): Reformulation-linearization technique cuts\n- **lp_primal_tolerance**, **lp_dual_tolerance** (double, default=1e-7, tags 266-267): Internal LP scaling tolerances\n\n## Presolve & Inprocessing\n- **inprocessing_use_congruence_closure** (bool, default=true, tag 342): Clausal congruence detection\n- **inprocessing_use_sat_sweeping** (bool, default=false, tag 354): \"Clausal Equivalence Sweeping\" algorithm (2025)\n- **load_at_most_ones_in_sat_presolve** (bool, default=false, tag 335): Constraint detection integration\n\n## Proof Checking (New Feature Set)\n- **check_lrat_proof**, **output_lrat_proof** (bool, tags 344, 345): LRAT proof validation\n- **check_drat_proof**, **output_drat_proof** (bool, tags 346, 347): DRAT proof support\n- **max_drat_time_in_seconds** (double, default=inf, tag 348): Proof verification timeout\n\n## Search & Linearization\n- **create_1uip_boolean_during_icr** (bool, default=true, tag 341): Integer conflict resolution enhancement\n- **use_new_integer_conflict_resolution** (bool, default=false, tag 336): Experimental conflict handling"}]},"uuid":"dc2438dc-947e-43c1-b6c4-34999d1252eb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:37.129Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d56721f-c474-4eea-8d92-727364e2b30f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
