{"parentUuid":"a84ab3ca-7ff9-4efe-8e8d-d60e8f8c4ab1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"acb4e62e0c603bceb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D44Me6HSfT2NcLEHjAL2Qk","type":"tool_result","content":"# Breaking Change in CpSolver.Solve() Callback\n\nBased on the GitHub issue, the breaking change involves a parameter rename:\n\n**Old Signature (Expected):**\n```python\nsolver.Solve(model, solution_callback=MyCallback())\n```\n\n**New Signature (Current):**\n```python\nsolver.solve(model, callback=MyCallback())\n```\n\n## The Issue\n\nThe deprecation of `CpSolver.Solve()` in favor of `.solve()` included an unintended parameter rename. The argument previously named `solution_callback` was accidentally renamed to `callback`. \n\nAs the issue reporter states: \"it seems like a mistake has been made here, accidentally renaming argument `solution_callback` to `callback`.\"\n\nThe old capitalized method `.Solve()` no longer accepts the `solution_callback` parameter, throwing a `TypeError` instead. While the new `.solve()` method works with the renamed parameter, this breaks backward compatibility for code still using the deprecated `.Solve()` method with its original parameter name."}]},"uuid":"3255d8af-e505-4190-b35f-d61d6afb2a7c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:46.957Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a84ab3ca-7ff9-4efe-8e8d-d60e8f8c4ab1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
